.TH str_copyn 3
.SH NAME
str_copyn \- copy a string with a limit
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <str.h>

size_t str_copyn(void* \fIp1\fP, const void* \fIp2\fP, size_t \fImax\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
str_copyn copies the null-terminated string from \fIp2\fP into \fIp1\fP,
copying at most \fImax\fP bytes. If the source is longer than \fImax\fP,
the result is truncated and null-terminated at the end of the buffer.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The number of bytes copied (excluding the null terminator).